---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: "Year-Round Shareable Pages | Pikes Peak Web Designs"
description: "Eight year-round pages, one for each moment most service businesses meet during the year. Share them on social media, in group replies, or by email."
noindex: true
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---

<section class="page-hero page-hero--peak">
  <div class="container">
    <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span>Seasons</span>
    </nav>
    <span class="section-label">Share-on-occasion pages</span>
    <h1>A page for each season, <em>ready to share</em></h1>
    <p>Here are eight year-round pages, one for each moment most service businesses meet during the year. Each page keeps the same address, so you can share the same link every January, every fall, and every Black Friday. Each is written for its moment instead of as a general pitch.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:1100px">
    <div class="seasons-grid">
      {% for s in seasons %}
        <a href="/seasons/{{ s.slug }}/" class="seasons-card">
          <span class="seasons-card-tag">{{ s.season }}</span>
          <h2 class="seasons-card-title">{{ s.h1 }} <em>{{ s.h1Em }}</em></h2>
          <p class="seasons-card-desc">{{ s.metaDescription }}</p>
          <span class="seasons-card-cta">Open the page &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--cream">
  <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
    <div class="text-center">
      <span class="section-label">How to use them</span>
      <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-inline:auto">Three ways to use the pages</h2>
    </div>
    <ol class="next-steps" style="margin-top:2rem">
      <li class="next-step">
        <span class="next-step-num">1</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Paste the link into a Facebook group reply</h3>
          <p>When someone in a trades Facebook group asks, "Should I get a new website?", paste the page for the season. It reads as a thoughtful answer instead of an ad, and the link is short enough for any character limit.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="next-step">
        <span class="next-step-num">2</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Add the link to an Instagram or LinkedIn post</h3>
          <p>Each page has a clean preview card, so the link displays properly on every social platform, including Instagram bio links, LinkedIn posts, and Twitter / X.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="next-step">
        <span class="next-step-num">3</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Send the link in an email or a text</h3>
          <p>Each page takes about two minutes to read on a phone. A link is easier to share than a pitch, and the page does the explaining for you.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cta-section">
  <div class="cta-inner">
    <span class="section-label">Ready for your own site?</span>
    <h2>Your new site, live in two to three weeks</h2>
    <p>These pages work all year. When you're ready for your own site, the build takes two to three weeks, at $175 a month with $0 down.</p>
    <div class="cta-buttons">
      <a href="/subscribe/" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg">Start now</a>
    </div>
    <p style="margin-top:1.25rem"><a href="/contact/" class="inline-link" style="color:var(--gold-400)">Prefer to talk first? Book a free call</a> (20 to 30 minutes on Google Meet).</p>
  </div>
</section>
